{"connection_id": "BC-1a65cda1b48ae7489da3", "ref": "WLC:Ezra.9.5", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "evening offering; kneeling; spread hands", "note": "At the evening offering Ezra rises from his self-affliction, falls to his knees, and spreads his hands to God. Its timed and bodily prayer scene closely meets the commentary's descriptions of salat."}
{"connection_id": "BC-80560b23d602fd7fc825", "ref": "WLC:Gen.14.20", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "God Most High; blessing", "note": "Melchizedek blesses God Most High after deliverance; the explicit divine title and blessing give a close Hebrew-Bible counterpart to the commentary's Lord Most High whose name is glorified."}
{"connection_id": "BC-bd52ae02660fb87cfe3e", "ref": "WLC:Isa.1.15", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "outspread hands; many prayers; violence", "note": "God refuses many prayers while the worshippers' hands are full of blood; this gives a pointed ethical counterpart to the commentary's claim that prayer turns people away from indecency and wrong."}
{"connection_id": "BC-ddfafcd937f9c61d5341", "ref": "WLC:Isa.12.4", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "thanks and calling on the name", "note": "The people give thanks, call on YHWH's name, and proclaim that his name is exalted; the verse binds invocation, praise, and public announcement in one liturgical act."}
{"connection_id": "BC-4f4a8344292414a6646e", "ref": "WLC:Isa.26.8", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "yearning for name and memorial", "note": "The community says its desire is for God's name and memorial while waiting for him; this makes remembrance of the name an inward devotion as well as speech."}
{"connection_id": "BC-cd451579deb18dfac8bc", "ref": "WLC:Isa.29.13", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "lips honoring while the heart is distant", "note": "Isaiah condemns people whose lips honor God while their hearts are far away; this sharpens the distinction between spoken devotion and inward reality that the commentary develops through loud and hidden."}
{"connection_id": "BC-c167235bbd06100a6e1d", "ref": "WLC:Isa.29.13", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "lips honoring God; heart far away", "note": "Isaiah distinguishes lip-honor from a distant heart; it illuminates the commentary's insistence that tesbih involves word, action, and intention, and its warning about heedless prayer."}
{"connection_id": "BC-067486474c08699f07cf", "ref": "WLC:Isa.56.7", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "house of prayer; accepted offerings", "note": "God's house is called a house of prayer for all peoples, where offerings are accepted. This directly pairs prayer with formal communal worship, an important aspect of the commentary's unified tesbih, dhikr, and salat."}
{"connection_id": "BC-e66641f4772dd6957bd9", "ref": "WLC:Isa.57.15", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "the high and lifted One; holy Name; reviving the lowly", "note": "Isaiah calls God high and lifted up, whose name is Holy, and says that he revives the contrite. This joins the Most High epithet to a divine restoring action relevant to the commentary's praise and purification pairing."}
{"connection_id": "BC-ee9aa485a09e5cde4cfb", "ref": "WLC:Isa.6.3", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "threefold holy acclamation; glory filling earth", "note": "The seraphim's antiphonal holy acclamation is a heavenly praise formula for YHWH. It offers a liturgical setting for the commentary's tesbih of the transcendent Lord, though it does not reproduce its prayer sequence."}
{"connection_id": "BC-4e2692001f3151efe18e", "ref": "WLC:Jonah.2.10", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "voice of thanksgiving; sacrifice; vowed act", "note": "Jonah promises sacrifice with a voice of thanksgiving and the fulfilment of vows. This compactly combines vocal praise, gratitude, ritual action, and obedience, all senses the commentary assigns to dhikr and tesbih."}
{"connection_id": "BC-2a949810fbc38cdea1af", "ref": "WLC:Josh.1.8", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "book in the mouth; meditation; doing", "note": "Joshua is to keep the Torah-book in his mouth, meditate on it day and night, and do it; this closely parallels the commentary's inclusion of recitation, tongue, intention, and obedient action within remembrance."}
{"connection_id": "BC-69239ab8c5b0b9172940", "ref": "WLC:Lam.3.41", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "lifting heart with hands to God", "note": "Lamentations calls for lifting both heart and hands to God. The explicit union of inward disposition and visible bodily action sharpens the commentary's word-action-intention account of prayer."}
{"connection_id": "BC-6dd1a8fbeb4f1e29aa86", "ref": "WLC:Lev.22.32", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "holy Name; God sanctifying Israel", "note": "The verse forbids profaning the holy Name and calls God the one who sanctifies Israel, sharpening the commentary's 14–15 linkage between a worshipper's prayer and God's purifying action."}
{"connection_id": "BC-ff27c3153afb20d2e52a", "ref": "WLC:Mal.1.11", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Name, sunrise and sunset, pure offering", "note": "Malachi makes YHWH's name great from sunrise to sunset and connects it with incense and a pure offering; it gathers the commentary's daily praise, Name, ritual action, and 14–15 purification link."}
{"connection_id": "BC-81f81394c80f6ed77e94", "ref": "WLC:Mal.3.16", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "speech, remembrance, and name", "note": "Those who fear YHWH speak with one another, and a memorial book is written for those who esteem his name; this combines spoken remembrance and honoring the name."}
