{"connection_id": "BC-411ea4d4623dda6ca15b", "ref": "WLC:Neh.8.6", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "blessing the great God; bowing and face-to-ground worship", "note": "Ezra blesses YHWH the great God, and the assembly answers, raises hands, bows, and worships with faces to the ground; it is a compact public analogue to praise, utterance, and bodily prayer together."}
