{"connection_id": "BC-1f31bdaa454a0c9d983c", "ref": "WLC:Neh.8.8", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "public reading and explanation", "note": "The Levites read the Torah and explain its sense so hearers understand; this concretely joins recitation and admonition, which the commentary places between the opening command and final prayer."}
{"connection_id": "BC-696566b6ad0b9421c324", "ref": "WLC:Neh.9.3", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "reading followed by confession and worship", "note": "The community spends one part of the day reading the Torah and another confessing and worshiping YHWH; this concretely joins recitation and prayer in one service."}
{"connection_id": "BC-c16035ae82eabfbd25dd", "ref": "WLC:Neh.9.3", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Torah reading, confession, worship", "note": "The people stand to read Torah and then confess and worship; this concretely parallels the commentary's claim that recitation, admonitory remembrance, and prayer belong to the same devotional work."}
{"connection_id": "BC-0ff1160ea71a4747a21b", "ref": "WLC:Neh.9.5", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "standing blessing of the name", "note": "The Levites tell the assembly to stand and bless YHWH forever, then bless his glorious name; this joins bodily worship and praise of the name as in the commentary's opening and closing act."}
{"connection_id": "BC-321c3ac56e92512455e7", "ref": "WLC:Ps.100.4", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "thanksgiving, praise, blessing the Name", "note": "Entering God's courts entails thanksgiving and praise, then giving thanks to him and blessing his name. The verse closely joins the commentary's dhikr as praise and thanks with public worship of the Name."}
{"connection_id": "BC-161c092623ca6dd3d371", "ref": "WLC:Ps.103.2", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "praise and not forgetting", "note": "The speaker blesses YHWH and tells his own soul not to forget God's benefits; this links praise with deliberate remembrance, including the commentary's concern with forgetting."}
{"connection_id": "BC-12ebd6cbff159ba770d4", "ref": "WLC:Ps.103.3", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "praise with deliberate non-forgetting", "note": "The verse tells the soul to bless YHWH and not forget his benefits; this is a distinct remembrance claim supporting the commentary's link between worship and avoiding forgetfulness."}
{"connection_id": "BC-a8f53982fa3833aeeec6", "ref": "WLC:Ps.113.2", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "bless the name forever", "note": "The name of YHWH is blessed “from now and forever”; this gives the same enduring verbal praise of the name urged by the commentary."}
{"connection_id": "BC-529411c810f52bb25c7d", "ref": "WLC:Ps.113.3", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "praise from dawn to dusk", "note": "The psalm calls for the name to be praised from sunrise to sunset; this makes name-praise a repeated daily practice."}
{"connection_id": "BC-64807c6d1a6870dd7552", "ref": "WLC:Ps.113.3", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Name praised from sunrise to sunset", "note": "The commentary invokes praise before sunrise and before sunset; this verse explicitly makes the praise of YHWH's name extend from the sun's rising to its setting."}
{"connection_id": "BC-c9a32f00653161ecb35d", "ref": "WLC:Ps.117.1", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "soydas", "basis": "Arabic س ب ح (B001); Hebrew שׁבח", "note": "The commentary labels Arabic س ب ح as B001. Psalm 117 uses the Hebrew Piel imperative שַׁבְּחוּהוּ, “praise him,” a likely Semitic cognate in a summons for all peoples to praise YHWH."}
{"connection_id": "BC-5e89b821ba8ab9617328", "ref": "WLC:Ps.119.16", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "not forgetting God's word", "note": "The psalmist vows not to forget God's word; this is a direct, text-specific counterpart to the commentary's recitation, non-forgetting, and later reminder within the surah's devotional sequence."}
{"connection_id": "BC-abc55fed0f82367afaaf", "ref": "WLC:Ps.119.171", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "lips pouring out praise after instruction", "note": "The psalmist's lips pour out praise because God teaches statutes. It specifically joins a tongue-level act of praise to received teaching, as the commentary joins Qur'an recitation and dhikr."}
{"connection_id": "BC-af752d3b374aa1390f35", "ref": "WLC:Ps.119.172", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "tongue singing God's word", "note": "The psalmist's tongue sings God's word; this is a precise oral-scriptural parallel to the commentary's statement that reading the Qur'an belongs to remembrance."}
{"connection_id": "BC-948a26432b41a4ef3e3a", "ref": "WLC:Ps.134.3", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "raised hands blessing YHWH", "note": "The night worshipers lift their hands in the sanctuary and bless YHWH; this is a bodily form of the praise the commentary gathers under prayer."}
{"connection_id": "BC-f2329593e8a87f1ec9cd", "ref": "WLC:Ps.135.13", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "soydas", "basis": "Hebrew זכר and the enduring name", "note": "The verse says YHWH's name and memorial endure through generations; זכר is cognate with the commentary's ذ ك ر label, and directly couples name with remembrance."}
{"connection_id": "BC-da2ac8fedc46a05b5ce0", "ref": "WLC:Ps.135.13", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "name and memorial through generations", "note": "The psalm places YHWH's enduring name beside his memorial through all generations; this gives a scriptural counterpart to remembering the Lord's name."}
{"connection_id": "BC-9e1893b32493386884ad", "ref": "WLC:Ps.139.5", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "word known before the tongue", "note": "The psalm says YHWH knows a word before it is on the speaker's tongue; this closely matches the claim that God knows what is voiced and concealed."}
{"connection_id": "BC-b0e0639c732e979c30d6", "ref": "WLC:Ps.141.2", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "prayer as incense; lifted hands as evening offering", "note": "Prayer is likened to incense and raised hands to the evening offering. It supplies a concrete bodily and time-marked analogue to the commentary's prayer as supplication and enacted worship."}
{"connection_id": "BC-af6f716193fe2f420c1c", "ref": "WLC:Ps.141.3", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "prayer as incense and lifted hands", "note": "The speaker asks that his prayer rise like incense and his lifted hands like an evening offering; this brings spoken supplication and bodily worship into one ritual image."}
{"connection_id": "BC-c08da3d899fdcd84fad3", "ref": "WLC:Ps.145.21", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "mouth blessing the holy name", "note": "The psalm ends with the speaker's mouth praising YHWH and all flesh blessing his holy name forever; this joins tongue and name-praise."}
{"connection_id": "BC-8e64d527c96842037838", "ref": "WLC:Ps.145.3", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "daily blessing of the name", "note": "The speaker blesses God every day and praises his name forever; this links remembrance and prayer to ongoing praise rather than a single utterance."}

item.stdout:
{"connection_id": "BC-83b3d2d97c199b2e82fb", "ref": "WLC:Ps.145.5", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "praise transmitted generation to generation", "note": "One generation is to praise God's works to the next and declare his mighty acts; this is a specific form of recitation and reminder."}
{"connection_id": "BC-199a0cf4b073e5b585c0", "ref": "WLC:Ps.148.13", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "praise the exalted name", "note": "The psalm says to praise YHWH's name because it alone is exalted; this directly meets the commentary's command to glorify the Lord's name, “the Most High.”"}
{"connection_id": "BC-4096ab219dfca9c26e41", "ref": "WLC:Ps.150.6", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "all breath praising YHWH", "note": "The psalm closes by calling everything that has breath to praise YHWH; this makes praise an embodied act, fitting the commentary's broad account of tasbih as word and deed."}
{"connection_id": "BC-316c4b802af6a6dd54d6", "ref": "WLC:Ps.19.15", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "mouth's words and heart's meditation", "note": "The prayer asks that both spoken words and inward meditation be acceptable to YHWH; it joins the audible and hidden dimensions of devotion."}
{"connection_id": "BC-4b86bfb1698316ab2e14", "ref": "WLC:Ps.20.9", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "soydas", "basis": "Hebrew זכר, invoking the name", "note": "The Hebrew verb נַזְכִּיר derives from זכר, cognate with the commentary's Arabic ذ ك ر label; here it means invoking the name of YHWH, not merely recalling information."}
{"connection_id": "BC-ad5cb5917b00256b1f84", "ref": "WLC:Ps.20.9", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "remembering the divine name", "note": "The worshiper says “we invoke the name of YHWH our God”; this is a close verbal counterpart to remembering the Lord's name before prayer in 87:15."}
{"connection_id": "BC-02dd0a0c5ab2665854cb", "ref": "WLC:Ps.30.5", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "soydas", "basis": "Hebrew זכר, memorial of holiness", "note": "The Hebrew calls for thanks to God's holy memorial, using זכר, cognate with the commentary's ذ ك ر label; remembrance here is voiced praise."}
{"connection_id": "BC-fb8f047e4835f295c08c", "ref": "WLC:Ps.63.7", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "soydas", "basis": "Hebrew זכר, remembering God", "note": "The Hebrew זכר (“remember”) is cognate with the commentary's Arabic ذ ك ر label; the psalm uses it for remembering God in bed."}
{"connection_id": "BC-b15f364f6fa12733e25e", "ref": "WLC:Ps.63.7", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "night remembrance and meditation", "note": "The speaker remembers God on his bed and meditates during the night watches; this develops remembrance as sustained inner devotion, alongside the commentary's spoken remembrance."}
{"connection_id": "BC-3ed4cc50dffa48d22317", "ref": "WLC:Ps.86.13", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "whole-hearted praise of God's name", "note": "The speaker thanks God with the whole heart and glorifies his name forever; this joins inward intention and praise of the name."}
{"connection_id": "BC-85e0f6648623741c22fb", "ref": "WLC:Ps.95.6", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "bowing before the maker", "note": "The worshipers bow and kneel before YHWH, their maker; this supplies the bodily prostration the commentary includes in prayer, in a creation-focused setting."}
{"connection_id": "BC-0d6e1dca5c2fd16442b8", "ref": "WLC:Ps.95.6", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "bowing and kneeling before the Maker", "note": "The psalm's invitation to worship, bow down, and kneel gives named bodily acts corresponding to the commentary's standing, bowing, prostration, and supplication as prayer."}
{"connection_id": "BC-f2e090873da2dc1afa49", "ref": "WLC:Ps.96.2", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "daily proclamation of the name", "note": "The worshiper is told to bless YHWH's name and announce his salvation day after day; this joins repeated remembrance with public praise."}
{"connection_id": "BC-732a36e1b83419e8bc5d", "ref": "WLC:Ps.96.2", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "singing to YHWH; blessing the Name day by day", "note": "The psalm commands singing to YHWH, blessing his name, and proclaiming salvation from day to day; it supplies a distinct psalmic formulation of the commentary's vocal praise, Name, recitation, and recurring practice."}
{"connection_id": "BC-31b7f9b187a2043c1a19", "ref": "WLC:Ps.96.8", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "glory due the name and an offering", "note": "Worshipers ascribe YHWH glory due his name and bring an offering into his courts; this places name-praise and ritual action together."}
{"connection_id": "BC-eff7dc9fc4cb20776faa", "ref": "WLC:Ps.97.12", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "soydas", "basis": "Hebrew זכר, praise at God's memorial", "note": "The verse joins singing to YHWH with giving thanks at the memorial of his holiness; its זכר noun is cognate with the commentary's ذ ك ر label."}
{"connection_id": "BC-f9b98cece13ad94cae67", "ref": "WLC:Ps.99.3", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "praise the holy name", "note": "The congregation praises YHWH's great and awesome name and calls him holy; the name itself is the object of worship as in 87:1."}
{"connection_id": "BC-4f2bd513ec83c9f2066b", "ref": "WLC:Ps.99.5", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "exaltation and bowing", "note": "The verse commands exalting YHWH and bowing at his footstool; it places praise and bodily prostration together, as the commentary does for tasbih and prayer."}
{"connection_id": "BC-382e2ef65056ef3185a7", "ref": "WLC:Zeph.3.9", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "purified speech; calling on the Name; united service", "note": "God gives peoples a purified lip so that they may call on YHWH's name and serve together; it links the commentary's tongue-bound dhikr, purification, and obedient worship without reducing them to mere speech."}

