{"id":"S087-TEV-MTF-002","gelenek":"tevrat","tur":"motif","ayet":"87:1|87:15","islev":"destek","iliski":"tematik","durum":"cikarim","kat":"temel","metin":"Nehemya 8:6'da Ezra Rabbe bereket diler; topluluk ellerini kaldırıp iki kez Âmin der ve yüzüstü eğilir: {he:וַיִּקְּדוּ וַיִּשְׁתַּחֲווּ לַיהוָה אַפַּיִם אָרְצָה, tr:vayyikkedû vayyishtaḥavvû la-Adonay appayim artzâ, gloss:yüzleri yere dönük Rabbe eğilip secde ettiler, source:WLC:Neh.8.6}. Övgü, karşılık veren ses ve bedenin hareketi tek toplu sahnedir.","kaynak":"WLC:Neh.8.6","paragraf":44,"capa":"Namaz bedensel bir iştir","bag":"benzerlik","tarihleme":"kuran_oncesi","nusha":"masoretik"}
{"id":"S087-TEV-MTF-003","gelenek":"tevrat","tur":"motif","ayet":"87:7|87:15","islev":"anlam_alani","iliski":"tematik","durum":"cikarim","kat":"ek","metin":"1 Samuel 1:13'te Hanna {he:רַק שְׂפָתֶיהָ נָּעוֹת וְקוֹלָהּ לֹא יִשָּׁמֵעַ, tr:rak sefatêha naot ve-kolâ lo yişşamea, gloss:yalnız dudakları oynuyor, sesi duyulmuyordu, source:WLC:1Sam.1.13} biçiminde dua eder. Bu sahne, sesli okuma ve ibadetten söz edilirken anmanın işitilebilirlik derecesinin değişebileceğini somutlaştırır.","kaynak":"WLC:1Sam.1.13","paragraf":44,"capa":"Yedinci ayetteki \"açık\" kelimesinin","bag":"benzerlik","tarihleme":"kuran_oncesi","nusha":"masoretik"}
{"id":"S087-TEV-MTF-004","gelenek":"tevrat","tur":"motif","ayet":"87:15","islev":"destek","iliski":"tematik","durum":"cikarim","kat":"ek","metin":"Daniel 6:11'de Daniel günde üç kez diz çöker, dua eder ve Tanrı'ya şükreder: {he:בָּרֵךְ עַל־בִּרְכוֹהִי וּמְצַלֵּא וּמוֹדֵא, tr:bârek al-birkohî u-metsallê u-modê, gloss:dizleri üzerine çöküp dua ediyor ve şükrediyordu, source:WLC:Dan.6.11}. Aramice ayet, bedensel duruşu ve övgüyü tekrarlanan dua pratiğinde birleştirir.","kaynak":"WLC:Dan.6.11","paragraf":44,"capa":"Namaz bedensel bir iştir","bag":"benzerlik","tarihleme":"kuran_oncesi","nusha":"masoretik"}
{"id":"S087-INC-MTF-004","gelenek":"incil","tur":"motif","ayet":"87:15","islev":"destek","iliski":"tematik","durum":"cikarim","kat":"ek","metin":"Luka 18:13'te vergi görevlisi uzakta durur, gözlerini kaldırmaz, göğsüne vurur ve {el:Ὁ θεός, ἱλάσθητί μοι τῷ ἁμαρτωλῷ, tr:ho theos hilasthēti moi tō hamartōlō, gloss:Tanrım, günahkâr olan bana merhamet et, source:SBLGNT:Luke.18.13} der. Dua, bedenin tutumu ile yakarışın bir aradalığı olarak anlatılır.","kaynak":"SBLGNT:Luke.18.13","paragraf":44,"capa":"Namaz bedensel bir iştir","bag":"benzerlik","tarihleme":"kuran_oncesi","nusha":"yunanca_ahit"}
{"id":"S087-INC-MTF-005","gelenek":"incil","tur":"motif","ayet":"87:7|87:15","islev":"destek","iliski":"tematik","durum":"cikarim","kat":"ek","metin":"1 Korintliler 14:25'te kalbin gizledikleri açığa çıkınca kişi yüzüstü düşüp Tanrı'ya tapar ve onun orada olduğunu ilan eder: {el:πεσὼν ἐπὶ πρόσωπον προσκυνήσει τῷ θεῷ, tr:pesōn epi prosōpon proskynēsei tō theō, gloss:yüzüstü düşüp Tanrı'ya tapacak, source:SBLGNT:1Cor.14.25}. Gizli olanın açılması, bedenin eğilmesi ve sözlü ikrar aynı sahnede yer alır.","kaynak":"SBLGNT:1Cor.14.25","paragraf":44,"capa":"Yedinci ayetteki \"açık\" kelimesinin","bag":"benzerlik","tarihleme":"kuran_oncesi","nusha":"yunanca_ahit"}
{"id":"S087-TEV-MTF-005","gelenek":"tevrat","tur":"motif","ayet":"87:1|87:15","islev":"destek","iliski":"tematik","durum":"cikarim","kat":"ek","metin":"Malaki 1:11'de Rabbin adının güneşin doğuşundan batışına dek büyük olduğu, adına her yerde buhur ve temiz sunu getirildiği söylenir: {he:מִמִּזְרַח־שֶׁמֶשׁ וְעַד־מְבוֹאוֹ גָּדוֹל שְׁמִי, tr:mi-mizrah şemeş ve-ad mevoo gadol şemî, gloss:güneşin doğuşundan batışına dek adım büyüktür, source:WLC:Mal.1.11}. Zaman, ad ve ibadet sunusu birlikte anılır; temiz olan burada sunudur.","kaynak":"WLC:Mal.1.11","paragraf":45,"capa":"Peygamber'e de","bag":"benzerlik","tarihleme":"kuran_oncesi","nusha":"masoretik"}
{"id":"S087-TEV-MTF-006","gelenek":"tevrat","tur":"motif","ayet":"87:15","islev":"karsit","iliski":"tematik","durum":"cikarim","kat":"ek","metin":"Yeşaya 29:13'te Tanrı, halkın kendisini dudaklarıyla onurlandırırken kalbini uzak tuttuğunu söyler: {he:בְּפִיו וּבִשְׂפָתָיו כִּבְּדוּנִי וְלִבּוֹ רִחַק מִמֶּנִּי, tr:befîv u-vi-sefatâv kibbedûnî ve-libbo riḥak mimmennî, gloss:ağız ve dudaklarıyla beni onurlandırdılar, fakat kalpleri benden uzaklaştı, source:WLC:Isa.29.13}. Bu karşı sahne, şerhin gafletli namaz ayrımına ağız ile yöneliş arasındaki mesafeyi ekler.","kaynak":"WLC:Isa.29.13","paragraf":45,"capa":"Namaz kılanlar arasında bile bir ayrım vardır","bag":"benzerlik","tarihleme":"kuran_oncesi","nusha":"masoretik"}
{"id":"S087-TEV-MTF-007","gelenek":"tevrat","tur":"motif","ayet":"87:6|87:9|87:15","islev":"destek","iliski":"yapisal","durum":"cikarim","kat":"temel","metin":"Nehemya 9:3'te topluluk günün bir bölümünü Tevrat kitabını okumaya, bir bölümünü de itiraf ve Rabbe secde etmeye ayırır: {he:וַיִּקְרְאוּ בְּסֵפֶר תּוֹרַת יְהוָה, tr:vayyikreû be-sefer torat Adonay, gloss:Rabbin Tevrat kitabından okudular, source:WLC:Neh.9.3}. Surede okuma ve öğüdün namaza uzanan dizilişiyle karşılaştırılabilecek somut bir ibadet akışıdır.","kaynak":"WLC:Neh.9.3","paragraf":45,"capa":"Kur'an bu üçlüyü sık sık birlikte sahneler","bag":"benzerlik","tarihleme":"kuran_oncesi","nusha":"masoretik"}
{"id":"S087-INC-MTF-006","gelenek":"incil","tur":"motif","ayet":"87:6|87:9|87:15","islev":"destek","iliski":"yapisal","durum":"cikarim","kat":"temel","metin":"Koloseliler 3:16, Mesih'in sözünün toplulukta yerleşmesini öğretme ve öğüt verme ile, ayrıca mezmurlar ve ilahiler söyleme ile yan yana koyar: {el:διδάσκοντες καὶ νουθετοῦντες ἑαυτοὺς ψαλμοῖς, tr:didaskontes kai nouthetountes heautous psalmois, gloss:birbirinize mezmurlarla öğreterek ve öğüt vererek, source:SBLGNT:Col.3.16}. Şerhteki okuma, öğüt ve övgü dizisine yakın bir toplu ibadet düzenidir.","kaynak":"SBLGNT:Col.3.16","paragraf":45,"capa":"Kur'an bu üçlüyü sık sık birlikte sahneler","bag":"benzerlik","tarihleme":"kuran_oncesi","nusha":"yunanca_ahit"}
{"id":"S087-INC-YGL-001","gelenek":"incil","tur":"yorum_gelenegi","ayet":"87:15","islev":"aciklama","iliski":"karsilastirmali","durum":"acik","kat":"ek","metin":"Matta 15:8–9'da İsa, Yeşaya'nın dudaklarla onurlandırma fakat kalbin uzak oluşu sözünü alıntılar ve insan buyruğuna dönüşen ibadeti boş sayar. Bu Hristiyan okuma, dışarıdan görülen ibadetin tek başına yeterli olmadığını belirginleştirir; şerhin namaz içindeki gaflet ayrımına bir karşılık verir.","kaynak":"SBLGNT:Matt.15.8|SBLGNT:Matt.15.9","paragraf":45,"capa":"Namaz kılanlar arasında bile bir ayrım vardır","bag":"benzerlik","tarihleme":"kuran_oncesi","nusha":"yunanca_ahit"}

payload.input:
text(await tools.apply_patch("*** Begin Patch
*** Add File: /Volumes/aro/projects/prose_generation/enrichment/bible/work/s087/ehlikitap-images.sol.max.session-20261005/sec11/verdicts.jsonl
+{"connection_id":"BC-1a2b6b312f482832e3c4","ref":"Didache 10.2","status":"unavailable","reason":"The named secondary text is absent from the frozen local snapshot; its proposed holy-name wording cannot be verified here.","paragraphs":[43],"evidence":[],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-7e68585e4fff2ef9bd85","ref":"Didache 8.2","status":"unavailable","reason":"The Didache passage is absent locally; the supposed prayer formula cannot be checked in this run.","paragraphs":[43],"evidence":[],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-51c085af138040152f4d","ref":"Didache 8.2","status":"unavailable","reason":"The local snapshot lacks this Didache witness, so its role as an early liturgical transmission is unverified.","paragraphs":[43],"evidence":[],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-d2a5249ff5e90b96731c","ref":"Didache 8.3","status":"unavailable","reason":"The thrice-daily prescription is not present in the local secondary-text snapshot.","paragraphs":[43],"evidence":[],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-7d9192f0a3e30ce5a83a","ref":"Didache 8.3","status":"unavailable","reason":"This Didache passage is absent locally; the specific liturgical reading remains unchecked.","paragraphs":[43],"evidence":[],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-875ec8347dcc1f6cbd2a","ref":"Justin Martyr, First Apology 67","status":"unavailable","reason":"Justin's named work is missing from the frozen source snapshot, so the proposed service sequence is not verified.","paragraphs":[43,45],"evidence":[],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-7d0d2e7cdfc82ed6ec50","ref":"SBLGNT:1Cor.14.15","status":"rejected","reason":"The verse joins prayer and psalmody in spirit and mind but does not connect either with the divine name; Heb 13:15 supplies the paragraph's specific lip-and-name motif.","paragraphs":[43],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1Cor.14.15"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-7a52c745998ee896d47e","ref":"SBLGNT:1Cor.14.15","status":"rejected","reason":"Spirit-and-mind prayer is a valid broad analogy, but the verse has no name invocation or bodily act and repeats the prayer-praise point more precisely made by Heb 13:15.","paragraphs":[43],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1Cor.14.15"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-a850696198ddd90856f4","ref":"SBLGNT:1Cor.14.16","status":"rejected","reason":"Paul's question concerns a listener's understanding and ability to answer Amen, not whether prayer is pronounced aloud as the paragraph's jahr point concerns.","paragraphs":[44],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1Cor.14.16"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-027588cae36301391c10","ref":"SBLGNT:1Cor.14.25","status":"accepted","reason":"The Greek explicitly moves from revealed heart-secrets to falling on the face, worship and spoken acknowledgement; this adds a compact hidden/bodily/voiced scene to paragraph 44.","paragraphs":[44],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1Cor.14.25"],"annotations":["S087-INC-MTF-005"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-4eec2e45cc973b5ff897","ref":"SBLGNT:1John.1.9","status":"rejected","reason":"The text joins confession of sins and divine cleansing, but contains no divine-name invocation or described prayer; Acts 22:16 addresses the name-and-cleansing pairing directly.","paragraphs":[43],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1John.1.9"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-afba0c2e922cfbd7845a","ref":"SBLGNT:1Thess.5.17","status":"rejected","reason":"The bare command to pray without ceasing lacks the name, praise, recitation and bodily features that distinguish this section.","paragraphs":[43,45],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1Thess.5.17"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-29f6a419b91f4ac9dddd","ref":"SBLGNT:1Thess.5.17","status":"rejected","reason":"Continual prayer gives frequency alone, whereas the section's comparison concerns how name-praise, reading and bodily prayer combine.","paragraphs":[43,45],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1Thess.5.17"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-74d7a6e7418bcc58324a","ref":"SBLGNT:1Thess.5.18","status":"rejected","reason":"Thanksgiving in all circumstances follows the prayer command but does not itself mention prayer or the name; the proposed pairing relies on a second verse.","paragraphs":[43],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1Thess.5.18"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-37a07015871100dbb5f6","ref":"SBLGNT:1Tim.2.1","status":"rejected","reason":"The Greek enumerates forms of petition and thanks, but the base already states that semantic range; this verse has no additional name or action sequence.","paragraphs":[43],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1Tim.2.1"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-39e5460e5d7488e41f4a","ref":"SBLGNT:1Tim.2.8","status":"rejected","reason":"Raised hands are genuine prayer posture, but Neh 8:6 also joins a bodily posture to audible communal praise and is more specific to this paragraph.","paragraphs":[44],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1Tim.2.8"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-72374478570b7fd446bd","ref":"SBLGNT:1Tim.2.8","status":"rejected","reason":"Anger and disputing qualify lifted-hands prayer, but the paragraph's wrong-doing line concerns a Qur'anic claim about prayer's effect; this Greek instruction supplies a different ethical relation.","paragraphs":[44,45],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1Tim.2.8"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-81d1630e259c342c1637","ref":"SBLGNT:Acts.10.4","status":"rejected","reason":"Prayers and alms rise as a memorial before God, but the memorial here is God's regard for Cornelius, not a worshipper's remembrance of God's name.","paragraphs":[43],"evidence":["SBLGNT:Acts.10.4"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-71254b806f32fa007128","ref":"SBLGNT:Acts.16.25","status":"rejected","reason":"Paul and Silas pray and sing hymns, a broad prayer-praise analogy already represented by the closer lip-and-name wording in Heb 13:15.","paragraphs":[43],"evidence":["SBLGNT:Acts.16.25"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-cf42d0ab69fe64261669","ref":"SBLGNT:Acts.16.25","status":"rejected","reason":"The prisoners' hearing establishes audibility, but the verse does not contrast open and hidden devotion; 1 Cor 14:25 supplies that added dimension.","paragraphs":[44],"evidence":["SBLGNT:Acts.16.25"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-d9750eee99d59f0db988","ref":"SBLGNT:Acts.2.21","status":"rejected","reason":"The Joel quotation links calling the Lord's name to salvation but does not pair invocation with prayer, praise or the surah's purification action.","paragraphs":[43],"evidence":["SBLGNT:Acts.2.21"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-dfba85ec2d02b4444c09","ref":"SBLGNT:Acts.2.42","status":"rejected","reason":"Apostolic teaching and prayers are listed together, but no recitation-to-reminder-to-worship movement is described as Neh 9:3 does.","paragraphs":[45],"evidence":["SBLGNT:Acts.2.42"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-900274f514344b0a81d2","ref":"SBLGNT:Acts.22.16","status":"accepted","reason":"The verse explicitly couples calling upon the name with baptismal washing from sins; the annotation states this limited parallel without equating baptism and salat.","paragraphs":[43],"evidence":["SBLGNT:Acts.22.16"],"annotations":["S087-INC-MTF-003"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-0fe1f334cf3d67e25170","ref":"SBLGNT:Acts.3.1","status":"rejected","reason":"The ninth-hour temple visit shows scheduled prayer but neither the named Lord nor praise, so it illustrates timing more than the section's central combination.","paragraphs":[43,45],"evidence":["SBLGNT:Acts.3.1"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-71994da0d55cafd1e26e","ref":"SBLGNT:Acts.7.59","status":"rejected","reason":"Stephen explicitly invokes Jesus during martyrdom; its Christological addressee and death scene are a less direct comparison to naming God before prayer in 87:15.","paragraphs":[43],"evidence":["SBLGNT:Acts.7.59"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-2f662ae377d84d9f53bd","ref":"SBLGNT:Acts.7.60","status":"rejected","reason":"Kneeling and loud intercession are present, but Luke 18:13 gives bodily supplication together with the inward humility relevant to the paragraph.","paragraphs":[44],"evidence":["SBLGNT:Acts.7.60"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-16f8be3bf109e3a308a3","ref":"SBLGNT:Col.3.16","status":"accepted","reason":"The Greek joins indwelling word, teaching, admonition, psalms and singing; this gives a close communal reading-to-praise sequence for paragraph 45.","paragraphs":[45],"evidence":["SBLGNT:Col.3.16"],"annotations":["S087-INC-MTF-006"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-a37e0435edae2823539f","ref":"SBLGNT:Col.3.16","status":"accepted","reason":"Admonition is explicitly combined with psalms and grateful singing, precisely the sequence expressed by the linked annotation.","paragraphs":[45],"evidence":["SBLGNT:Col.3.16"],"annotations":["S087-INC-MTF-006"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-828394334708e02ada68","ref":"SBLGNT:Col.3.17","status":"rejected","reason":"The verse relates word, deed, Jesus' name and thanks, but unlike 3:16 it lacks teaching or admonition and does not describe prayer; the proposed sequence is stronger in 3:16.","paragraphs":[43,45],"evidence":["SBLGNT:Col.3.17"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-0e4e1ab6b1295858d20f","ref":"SBLGNT:Col.4.2","status":"rejected","reason":"Persistence in prayer with thanks repeats the prayer-praise motif without the specific name, reading or bodily act discussed here.","paragraphs":[43],"evidence":["SBLGNT:Col.4.2"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-0c8c6d1f72a024f06b59","ref":"SBLGNT:Eph.5.19","status":"rejected","reason":"Psalms and hymns are spoken and sung, but Col 3:16 additionally names teaching and admonition, the feature needed for paragraph 45.","paragraphs":[43,45],"evidence":["SBLGNT:Eph.5.19"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-32de1da7ed096f4cd44c","ref":"SBLGNT:Eph.5.19","status":"rejected","reason":"Heart-singing adds inwardness but no prayer or name invocation; Col 3:16 covers the hymn motif and supplies the paragraph's teaching/reminder step.","paragraphs":[43,45],"evidence":["SBLGNT:Eph.5.19"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-cc55f3b846d98e270cf4","ref":"SBLGNT:Eph.5.20","status":"rejected","reason":"Thanks in Jesus' name is explicit but the verse does not describe prayer movements or name-praise itself; Matt 6:9 gives the latter in a prayer formula.","paragraphs":[43],"evidence":["SBLGNT:Eph.5.20"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-436fe931da86af05a6d8","ref":"SBLGNT:Heb.10.22","status":"rejected","reason":"Approach with cleansed hearts and washed bodies is not paired with explicit divine-name invocation or salat; Acts 22:16 is a closer name-and-cleansing comparison.","paragraphs":[43],"evidence":["SBLGNT:Heb.10.22"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-c1f9d3e58a3b1a099ec0","ref":"SBLGNT:Heb.13.15","status":"accepted","reason":"The Greek calls continual praise a sacrifice and defines it as the fruit of lips acknowledging God's name; it directly combines the paragraph's three motifs.","paragraphs":[43],"evidence":["SBLGNT:Heb.13.15"],"annotations":["S087-INC-MTF-002"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-4e62b8d4527de377702d","ref":"SBLGNT:Heb.13.15","status":"accepted","reason":"The text explicitly identifies praise with lips confessing the name, exactly as expressed in the linked annotation.","paragraphs":[43],"evidence":["SBLGNT:Heb.13.15"],"annotations":["S087-INC-MTF-002"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-cbc149ebcce22b2a5609","ref":"SBLGNT:Heb.13.16","status":"rejected","reason":"Doing good and sharing are sacrifices pleasing to God, but the verse no longer speaks of the divine name, recitation or prayer; it extends the preceding image beyond the section's focus.","paragraphs":[43],"evidence":["SBLGNT:Heb.13.16"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-c17c51993a8df3fd4625","ref":"SBLGNT:Jas.5.13","status":"rejected","reason":"James assigns prayer to suffering and psalm-singing to cheerfulness as alternative responses, so it does not combine praise and petition in one act as proposed.","paragraphs":[43],"evidence":["SBLGNT:Jas.5.13"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-e7ffb486b87088341479","ref":"SBLGNT:John.11.41","status":"rejected","reason":"Jesus thanks the Father before Lazarus' raising, but the verse lacks name invocation and any stated contrast of audible and concealed prayer.","paragraphs":[44],"evidence":["SBLGNT:John.11.41"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-3ef4ea40fff3fbe585bf","ref":"SBLGNT:John.11.42","status":"rejected","reason":"Jesus says he spoke for the crowd's belief; this qualifies a claim about public prayer's motive, but the base makes no claim that voiced prayer is wrong.","paragraphs":[44],"evidence":["SBLGNT:John.11.42"],"annotations":[]}
*** End Patch"));

